WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:09.474
Hi! A tissue box, a can, a ball: what shapes are they? Today we'll learn about 3D shapes.

2
00:00:09.624 --> 00:00:15.762
A cube is like a dice. It has 6 faces, and every face is the same square.

3
00:00:15.912 --> 00:00:22.194
A cuboid is like a tissue box. It also has 6 faces, mostly rectangles.

4
00:00:22.344 --> 00:00:28.362
A cylinder is like a can. Its top and bottom are circles, and the side is curved.

5
00:00:28.512 --> 00:00:38.274
A cone is like an ice-cream cone, with a circle at the bottom and a point at the top. A sphere is round with no flat faces.

6
00:00:38.424 --> 00:00:43.746
Shapes with a curved surface can roll, like spheres, cylinders and cones.

7
00:00:43.896 --> 00:00:50.250
Shapes with flat tops and bottoms can be stacked, like cubes, cuboids and cylinders.

8
00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:55.482
A cylinder is special: lying down it rolls, standing up it stacks.

9
00:00:55.632 --> 00:01:01.362
A sphere is curved everywhere, so it rolls but can't be stacked.

10
00:01:01.512 --> 00:01:05.394
Watch out! A tissue box is not a cube!

11
00:01:05.544 --> 00:01:11.850
All 6 faces of a cube are equal squares, but a tissue box has mostly rectangles.

12
00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:16.170
So a tissue box is a cuboid.

13
00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:24.786
Your turn! What 3D shape is a basketball? Pause and think.

14
00:01:24.936 --> 00:01:31.098
It's round with no flat faces: a sphere. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:31.248 --> 00:01:39.498
Another one! What 3D shape is a can? Pause and think.

16
00:01:39.648 --> 00:01:46.530
Circles on top and bottom, curved side: a cylinder. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:55.146
Here's another! How many faces does a cube have? Pause and think.

18
00:01:55.296 --> 00:02:00.666
A cube has 6 faces. Did you get it right?

19
00:02:00.816 --> 00:02:10.770
Try one more! Sphere, cylinder or cube: which one can't roll? Pause and think.

20
00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:17.490
A cube has only flat faces, so it can't roll. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:26.610
Try one more! What 3D shape is an ice-cream cone? Pause and think.

22
00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:33.258
Round at one end and pointed at the other: a cone. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:33.408 --> 00:02:41.994
Last one! Which shape can roll and also stack? Pause and think.

24
00:02:42.144 --> 00:02:48.714
A cylinder rolls lying down and stacks standing up. Did you get it right?

25
00:02:48.864 --> 00:03:03.522
Remember: a cube has 6 equal faces, a cuboid has 6 faces, a cylinder has circles top and bottom, a cone has a point, and a sphere has no flat faces. Curved surfaces roll, flat faces stack.

26
00:03:03.672 --> 00:03:09.114
Find five things at home and name their 3D shapes!

